From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: poll the noisy SD card-detect line

GPIO38 generates continuous spurious card-detect edges on SM-T531. Each
edge reports a five-second MMC wakeup event, and a new event during the
pre-suspend filesystem sync aborts system sleep with -EBUSY. A captured
failure turns the display off and immediately back on without suspending.

Use the existing broken-cd fallback instead of the GPIO IRQ. SDHCI disables
native card-detect interrupts, and MMC polls card presence/liveness once a
second while awake. This does not mark the socket non-removable, change
SD data/power IRQs, or suppress real system wakeup sources. Remove cd-gpios
so an unstable level cannot override the polling fallback. Keep the other
Matisse variants unchanged.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -108,6 +108,9 @@
 };
 
 &sdhc_2 {
+	/* GPIO38 produces spurious card-detect IRQs and aborts suspend. */
+	/delete-property/ cd-gpios;
+	broken-cd;
 	/* SDR104 currently fails sustained card I/O during bring-up. */
 	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	no-1-8-v;
